**Legacy RHEL 5/6 Server Migration to Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.3**

## Overview

Several legacy Linux servers running **RHEL 5.x and RHEL 6.7** had reached end of support and could not be upgraded in place. Since Red Hat supports
**in-place upgrades only from RHEL 7 onwards** using the Leapp utility, the only supported migration path was a **fresh installation** of 
**Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.3**.

The migration involved backing up application data, rebuilding the virtual machines with RHEL 9.3, recreating the existing server configuration, 
restoring the required application data, and validating the environment before handing it over to the application team.

