## Key Learning

Legacy operating systems such as **RHEL 5** and **RHEL 6** cannot be upgraded directly to modern Red Hat releases because in-place upgrade support 
begins with RHEL 7. A well-planned migration using a fresh installation, combined with comprehensive backups and recreation of the existing server 
configuration—including hostnames, IP addresses, mount points, users, swap, and NTP settings—ensures a smooth transition to a supported operating 
system with minimal impact on application functionality.
